 "id": "check.evidence_levels",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "engine_min": "1.1",
 "status": "active",
 "title": "Organic-evidence level (none / trace / clear / strong / can't tell) and score S",
 "description": "Normative rule of the frozen evidence study (PLAN v3.2 Step 7). E = -1e5 x SG31 cubic 2nd derivative of log10(1/max(R,1e-6)); band reading = mean E over centre +- half width; u_b = E_b / w_b (band centres, weights, faint thresholds and noise windows from bands.json). Band state: can't tell if sd_u > sd_max_u and u < unreadable_only_if_u_below; else strong (u >= strong), clear (u >= clear), faint (u > faint_b), flat. Lit = faint, clear or strong. S = median u over readable core bands (null if none readable). none: every core band flat or unreadable, the must-be-readable bands readable, >= min_readable_core readable, the extra band <= extra_band_max_u or unreadable (sd only), guard max E < max_E_below. can't tell: not none, no core band lit, guard passes, extra band not resolved-and-readable. strong: S >= strong, every readable core band lit, an N-H type band >= nh_type_min_u. clear: S >= clear, >= clear_min_lit_core lit, an N-H type band >= nh_type_min_u. trace: otherwise. Never a %. A band with a 'projection' in bands.json (NH1545c: the OH-corrected 1545 nm trough) is read on the projected window and u = u_sign x E / w.",
 "licence": "CC-BY-4.0",
 "created": "2026-10-03",
 "provenance": {
  "basis": "Frozen 2026-10-02 (Phase 0a A3; rule script hash 355dd063...). Weights = median band ratios over the 140 Ryder et al. 2026 reference bones >= 1% (public mmc2). Faint thresholds = 99th percentile of collagen-free archaeological fauna (unreleased data; statistics only, no site named). Guard set on bison bone (Ryder et al. 2026b, Archaeometry SI). Validation per spectrum: 0 of 72 spectra >= 3% yield called 'none' (one-sided 95% bound 4.1%).",
  "nh1545c": "Phase 0c (DECISIONS 75): the OH-corrected 1545 nm trough is a 5th core band (in S and in lit / flat, never an N-H-type band), lit line 1.5 u set on true-zero archaeological bone (no scan of the collagen-free reference layers exceeds 1.5 u). Across 3,280 scans it changes one verdict (a false evidence lift on an unflagged alkyd-coated scan) and no 'none' call on true-zero bone; the stress test (none at >= 3% / >= 1%) is unchanged."
 },
